prompt:
Extract the demurrage, detention, terminal storage and chassis terms that apply to a container at Los Angeles carried by MAERSK.

CONTRACT AND TARIFF TEXT
------------------------
SERVICE CONTRACT NO. SC-2026-0042  -  PORT OF LOS ANGELES / LONG BEACH

SECTION 7. FREE TIME AND DEMURRAGE
7.1 Merchant shall be allowed four (4) calendar days of free time for import
demurrage, counted from the day after the container is discharged from the
vessel and made available at the marine terminal.
7.2 After expiry of free time, demurrage shall accrue per container per day as
follows:
    Days 1-3 after LFD ..... USD 155 per day
    Days 4-6 after LFD ..... USD 310 per day
    Day 7 and thereafter ... USD 465 per day
Weekends and US federal holidays are counted as chargeable days.

SECTION 8. DETENTION / PER DIEM (EQUIPMENT)
8.1 Five (5) working days of free time are allowed for equipment detention,
counted from gate-out of the loaded container.
8.2 Detention thereafter accrues at USD 120 per container per day for days 1-5
and USD 200 per day thereafter.

SECTION 9. TERMINAL STORAGE
9.1 Terminal storage is billed separately by the marine terminal operator under
its published tariff and is not covered by this contract.

------------------------

Return free time in days and the full tier table for each charge type present.

Reply with ONE JSON object and nothing else - no prose, no markdown fences. Omit optional fields you cannot fill rather than inventing them, and do not add fields that are not listed. It must validate against this JSON schema:
{
  "$defs": {
    "ChargeType": {
      "enum": [
        "demurrage",
        "detention",
        "storage",
        "chassis"
      ],
      "title": "ChargeType",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "ClockTerms": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Free time plus tier table for a single charge type.",
      "properties": {
        "charge_type": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ChargeType"
        },
        "billed_by": {
          "title": "Billed By",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "free_days": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Free Days",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "tiers": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Tier"
          },
          "title": "Tiers",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "counts_weekends": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Counts Weekends",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "counts_holidays": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Counts Holidays",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "charge_type",
        "billed_by",
        "free_days",
        "tiers"
      ],
      "title": "ClockTerms",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Tier": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "One band of an escalating rate schedule.\n\n``from_day`` is inclusive and 1-based, counted from the first billed day.\n``to_day`` is inclusive; ``None`` means \"and everything after\".",
      "properties": {
        "from_day": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "From Day",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "to_day": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "minimum": 1,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "To Day"
        },
        "rate_usd": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "minimum": 0.0,
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "pattern": "^(?!^[-+.]*$)[+-]?0*\\d*\\.?\\d*$",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Rate Usd"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "from_day",
        "rate_usd"
      ],
      "title": "Tier",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "description": "Everything extracted from the service contract and terminal tariff.\n\nThis is the single highest-leverage object in the system: every later\ncalculation depends on it. ``confidence`` is emitted by the extraction\nactivity so low-confidence extractions can be routed to a human on day 1,\nwhen there is no time pressure.",
  "properties": {
    "contract_id": {
      "title": "Contract Id",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "port": {
      "title": "Port",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "carrier": {
      "title": "Carrier",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "clocks": {
      "additionalProperties": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/ClockTerms"
      },
      "propertyNames": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/ChargeType"
      },
      "title": "Clocks",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "confidence": {
      "default": 1.0,
      "maximum": 1.0,
      "minimum": 0.0,
      "title": "Confidence",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "source_document_id": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "title": "Source Document Id"
    },
    "extraction_notes": {
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "title": "Extraction Notes",
      "type": "array"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "contract_id",
    "port",
    "carrier",
    "clocks"
  ],
  "title": "ContractTerms",
  "type": "object"
}

